{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>When the camels had finished drinking.</b> This was necessarily some time after she had finished drawing, and he observed that she sought nothing in return, but all her deeds were of purely gratuitous kindness." "<b>And two bracelets upon her arms.</b> Fitting the measure of her arms, as in וְעָשִׂיתָ עַל הַחֹשֶׁן שַׁרְשֹׁת גַּבְלוּת (Exodus 28:22), וְעָשִׂיתָ עָלָיו זֵר זָהָב (Exodus 25:11) — fitting their measures."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:26.226854629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}